From: Beaverfffan <1056715226@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: add the RTL8366UB 802.1Q tagging protocol id

include/net/dsa.h is touched by several patches in sequence, and each of
them inserts its id right after DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_8021Q_VALUE. That
only works while every inserter sees the same context, so this patch is
deliberately numbered last (799-91).

Take a value well above the upstream sequence: 32 is already
DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_VALUE in v7.0 (master is at 35), so on the next kernel
bump both taggers would claim it.  Duplicate enumerators compile silently,
both drivers then carry the alias "dsa_tag:id-32", and
dsa_tag_driver_get_by_id() returns whichever driver registered first - link
order decides, with no warning, and the RTL8366UB CPU port would silently end
up with the MxL862 8-byte tagger.  Nothing indexes by proto value (the module
alias uses %d), so a value high above the sequence is safe until an id is
assigned on netdev.

Signed-off-by: Beaverfffan <1056715226@qq.com>
---

--- a/include/net/dsa.h
+++ b/include/net/dsa.h
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@
 #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_BRCM_LEGACY_FCS_VALUE	29
 #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_VALUE		30
 #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_8021Q_VALUE	31
+#define DSA_TAG_PROTO_RTL8366UB_8021Q_VALUE	200
 #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT921X_VALUE		33
 #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X_VALUE		34
 #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X_4B_VALUE		35
@@ -94,6 +95,7 @@
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_VSC73XX_8021Q	= DSA_TAG_PROTO_VSC73XX_8021Q_VALUE,
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862		= DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_VALUE,
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_8021Q	= DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_8021Q_VALUE,
+	DSA_TAG_PROTO_RTL8366UB_8021Q	= DSA_TAG_PROTO_RTL8366UB_8021Q_VALUE,
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT921X		= DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT921X_VALUE,
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X		= DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X_VALUE,
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X_4B		= DSA_TAG_PROTO_YT922X_4B_VALUE,
